    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This is a wonderful opportunity to purchase a detached three-bedroom bungalow in an excellent location close to Kells town centre.\n\nWhile in need of some updating, the property offers an ideal opportunity to create a home tailored to your own tastes in a highly convenient location. The property may also qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the purchaser meeting the relevant eligibility criteria.\n\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 95.5 sq.m. and includes an entrance hallway, kitchen/dining room, sitting room, three bedrooms and bathroom. Outside, there are mature lawned gardens to the front and rear, an attached garage and a tarmac driveway providing off-street parking. The generous rear garden is not overlooked, offering excellent privacy.\n\nThis property offers excellent potential for those seeking a home close to the amenities of Kells town.\n\nLOCATION \nThe property is located near Kells town centre and within easy access to the M3/M50. \nKells is one of Ireland`s most historic and vibrant heritage towns, offering an exceptional quality of life and an excellent range of amenities, including a selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools. The town boasts an excellent choice of sporting facilities, including the renowned Headfort Golf Club, a swimming pool, GAA, soccer and rugby clubs, together with a wide variety of shops, cafs, award-winning restaurants, traditional pubs and hotels.\n\nKells is also home to a thriving community and a rich cultural calendar, hosting events such as the acclaimed Hinterland Festival of Literature Arts and the Samhain Festival of Food Culture, both of which attract visitors from across the country.\n\nEntrance Hall\nBright hallway with wood laminate flooring.\n\nSitting Room\nFacing the front, the large window makes the room bright and light-filled, while an open fireplace, set within a black marble surround, adds character. Wood laminate flooring.\n\nKitchen\nTo the rear, there is a fitted kitchen with plenty of storage and a peninsula breakfast bar providing additional seating. Open plan to the dining room, there is potential to reconfigure the space into a large open-plan family kitchen/dining room. Linoleum flooring. Doors lead to the rear garden and garage.\n\nDining Room\nOpen plan to the kitchen with plenty of space for a family dining table. Linoleum flooring.\n\nBedroom 1\nTo the front, spacious room with linoleum flooring.\n\nBedroom 2\nTo the rear, a bright and spacious room with a large window and linoleum flooring. Wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 3\nTo the front with fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom\nTo the rear. Bath, separate electric shower, w.c. and w.h.b.\n\nGarage\nLarge garage with up and over door, direct access from the kitchen and a door leading to the rear garden.\n\nOutdoors\nLawned gardens to the front and rear, with mature planting. The generous rear garden is not overlooked, offering excellent privacy.Tarmac driveway to the front.\n\n\nDirections\nFrom Kells travel out the Moynalty Road. Property is on the left hand side. Follow eircode A82 C3W5.\n\nwhat3words /// members.hooks.vixens\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
